WEBVTT

00:05.920 --> 00:11.590
Scientific notation is a real world application that gives us a convenient way to handle either really,

00:11.590 --> 00:15.340
really big numbers or really, really small numbers.

00:15.880 --> 00:20.860
It's a concept that combines together so much of what we've learned in this course, including signed

00:20.860 --> 00:25.780
numbers, fractions, decimals and exponents.

00:25.930 --> 00:30.340
We'll need to pull all of these concepts together to learn about scientific notation.

00:30.340 --> 00:32.260
So let's put our skills to the test.

00:32.560 --> 00:36.910
We'll start by introducing the concept of scientific notation, and then we'll learn how to convert

00:36.910 --> 00:40.510
other numbers into scientific notation and vice versa.
